From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niall Smart <niall.smart@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:31:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: pl061: skip irqchip setup when there is no parent irq

The driver already tolerates a missing parent interrupt, logging "IRQ support
disabled" and continuing.  It then registers the irqchip anyway, so
gpiochip_add_data() calls irq_set_chained_handler_and_data() with IRQ 0 and
warns with a backtrace.

On this board none of the nineteen PL061 banks has an interrupt described --
the vendor kernel does not use GPIO interrupts either -- so every bank
produced a backtrace at boot.  Only register the irqchip when a parent
interrupt actually exists.

This is a local hardware-enablement patch and is not for submission; an
upstream fix would want to distinguish "no interrupt described" from "failed
to get one".
---
 drivers/gpio/gpio-pl061.c | 20 +++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpio-pl061.c b/drivers/gpio/gpio-pl061.c
index 02e4ffcf5a6f..3fcfa151357c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-pl061.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-pl061.c
@@ -346,15 +346,17 @@ static int pl061_probe(struct amba_device *adev, const struct amba_id *id)
 	pl061->parent_irq = irq;
 
 	girq = &pl061->gc.irq;
-	gpio_irq_chip_set_chip(girq, &pl061_irq_chip);
-	girq->parent_handler = pl061_irq_handler;
-	girq->num_parents = 1;
-	girq->parents = devm_kcalloc(dev, 1, sizeof(*girq->parents),
-				     GFP_KERNEL);
-	if (!girq->parents)
-		return -ENOMEM;
-	girq->parents[0] = irq;
-	girq->default_type = IRQ_TYPE_NONE;
+	if (irq) {
+		gpio_irq_chip_set_chip(girq, &pl061_irq_chip);
+		girq->parent_handler = pl061_irq_handler;
+		girq->num_parents = 1;
+		girq->parents = devm_kcalloc(dev, 1, sizeof(*girq->parents),
+					     GFP_KERNEL);
+		if (!girq->parents)
+			return -ENOMEM;
+		girq->parents[0] = irq;
+		girq->default_type = IRQ_TYPE_NONE;
+	}
 	girq->handler = handle_bad_irq;
 
 	ret = devm_gpiochip_add_data(dev, &pl061->gc, pl061);
